Forgejo for Debian (freshdeb)
=============================

The layout follows upstream's installation guide
(https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/installation/binary/):

  /usr/bin/forgejo          the binary, with the web frontend built in
  /etc/forgejo/app.ini      the configuration, written by the install wizard
  /var/lib/forgejo          the work path: repositories, the SQLite database,
                            attachments, logs, custom/ for templates
  git                       the system user Forgejo runs as (home /home/git,
                            where SSH access keeps authorized_keys)

Forgejo looks for /etc/forgejo/app.ini and /var/lib/forgejo by default, so
"forgejo admin ...", "forgejo doctor ..." and the like work as user git
without --config or --work-path:

  sudo -u git forgejo admin user list

Installation
------------

The service isn't enabled on install: until the install wizard has been
completed, the first visitor to http://<host>:3000/ configures the instance
and creates its administrator. Start it when you're ready to do that, or
write /etc/forgejo/app.ini yourself first (with INSTALL_LOCK = true):

  systemctl enable --now forgejo

The wizard needs to write /etc/forgejo/app.ini, so /etc/forgejo is writable
by git (root:git 0770) at first. Once the installation is done, make it
read-only for Forgejo, as upstream's guide says:

  chmod 750 /etc/forgejo
  chmod 640 /etc/forgejo/app.ini

Upgrades migrate the database forward; there is no way back, so take a
backup ("forgejo dump") before a new major (see NEWS.Debian).

Purging the package removes nothing of the instance: /etc/forgejo/app.ini
holds the secrets (SECRET_KEY) that parts of /var/lib/forgejo are encrypted
with, so both stay, and so does the git user. Delete them by hand to start
over.
